  "bug_info": "Summary of configuration for Project: Math\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Script dir: /root/defects4j/framework\n      Base dir: /root/defects4j\n    Major root: /root/defects4j/major\n      Repo dir: /root/defects4j/project_repos\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Project ID: Math\n       Program: commons-math\n    Build file: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Math/Math.build.xml\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n           Vcs: Vcs::Git\n    Repository: /root/defects4j/project_repos/commons-math.git\n     Commit db: /root/defects4j/framework/projects/Math/active-bugs.csv\nNumber of bugs: 106\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary for Bug: Math-33\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision ID (fixed version):\n3c4cb189cc91c5ca78cab3ba95dc82bee715d39a\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRevision date (fixed version):\n2012-05-02 18:28:37 +0000\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report id:\nMATH-781\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nBug report url:\nhttps://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/MATH-781\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRoot cause in triggering tests:\n - org.apache.commons.math3.optimization.linear.SimplexSolverTest::testMath781\n   --> junit.framework.AssertionFailedError\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nList of modified sources:\n - org.apache.commons.math3.optimization.linear.SimplexTableau\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------",
  "bug_report_content": "Title: SimplexSolver gives bad results\nType: Bug | Priority: Major | Status: Closed | Resolution: Fixed\n\nDescription:\nMethode SimplexSolver.optimeze(...) gives bad results with commons-math3-3.0\nin a simple test problem. It works well in commons-math-2.2.\n\nComments:\n\n[Luc Maisonobe]: Could you give some more information ?\n\nWhat is the simple problem ? What are the expected results ? What are the results returned by Apache Commons Math 3.0 ?\nCould we have some example code so we can reproduce the problem ?\n\n[Scheiber Ern\u0151]: Hi,\n\nI attached the test codes LinearProgCM.java for commons-math3-3.0 and \nLinearProgCM2.java for commons-math-2.2.\n\nBest regards,\nE.Scheiber\n\n[Thomas Neidhart]: I did a quick check and found no obvious reason for the different behavior. I will do a more thorough check when I am back in 2 weeks.\n\n[Thomas Neidhart]: in MATH-434, floating-point comparisons have been changed to use either an:\n\n * epsilon for any comparisons related to algorithm convergence\n * ulp for any other comparisons\n\nNow, when dropping the objective function of the first phase, the comparison is done using ulp which is wrong imho as it is basically a convergence check. When changing this back to an epsilon check like before, the test runs through as expected.\n\n[Thomas Neidhart]: The algorithm flow is as follows:\n\n * perform phase 1:\n ** iterate while !optimal\n ** isOptimal uses epsilon\n * after phase 1, drop phase 1 objective function\n ** drop columns using the same criteria as in isOptimal but with ulp instead of epsilon\n * perform phase 2\n ** ..\n\nAfter finishing phase 1, we end up dropping columns based on a different epsilon (ulp) as in the convergence check of the iteration for phase 1.",
  "fix_diff": "--- org.apache.commons.math3.optimization.linear.SimplexTableau (buggy)\n+++ org.apache.commons.math3.optimization.linear.SimplexTableau (fixed)\n@@ -335,7 +335,7 @@\n         // positive cost non-artificial variables\n         for (int i = getNumObjectiveFunctions(); i < getArtificialVariableOffset(); i++) {\n             final double entry = tableau.getEntry(0, i);\n-            if (Precision.compareTo(entry, 0d, maxUlps) > 0) {\n+            if (Precision.compareTo(entry, 0d, epsilon) > 0) {\n                 columnsToDrop.add(i);\n             }\n         }"
